NNAAMMEE
     mmsskk — Marvell/SysKonnect Yukon II Gigabit Ethernet adapter driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee mmiiiibbuuss
           ddeevviiccee mmsskk

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           if_msk_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmsskk device driver provides support for various NICs based on the Mar‐
     vell/SysKonnect Yukon II Gigabit Ethernet controller chip.

     All NICs supported by the mmsskk driver have TCP/UDP/IP checksum offload for
     transmit, TCP segmentation offload (TSO), hardware VLAN tag stripping/in‐
     sertion features and an interrupt moderation mechanism as well as a
     64-bit multicast hash filter.  The Yukon II supports TBI (ten bit inter‐
     face) and GMII transceivers, which means it can be used with either cop‐
     per or 1000baseX fiber applications.

     The Yukon II also supports Jumbo Frames (up to 9022 bytes), which can be
     configured via the interface MTU setting.  Selecting an MTU larger than
     1500 bytes with the ifconfig(8) utility configures the adapter to receive
     and transmit Jumbo Frames.

     The mmsskk driver supports the following media types:

     aauuttoosseelleecctt   Enable autoselection of the media type and options.  The
                  user can manually override the autoselected mode by adding
                  media options to rc.conf(5).

     1100bbaasseeTT//UUTTPP  Set 10Mbps operation.  The ifconfig(8) mmeeddiiaaoopptt option can
                  also be used to select either ffuullll--dduupplleexx or hhaallff--dduupplleexx
                  modes.

     110000bbaasseeTTXX    Set 100Mbps (Fast Ethernet) operation.  The ifconfig(8)
                  mmeeddiiaaoopptt option can also be used to select either
                  ffuullll--dduupplleexx or hhaallff--dduupplleexx modes.

     11000000bbaasseeTTXX   Set 1000baseTX operation over twisted pair.  The ifconfig(8)
                  mmeeddiiaaoopptt option can also be used to select either
                  ffuullll--dduupplleexx or hhaallff--dduupplleexx modes.

     11000000bbaasseeSSXX   Set 1000Mbps (Gigabit Ethernet) operation.  Both ffuullll--dduupplleexx
                  and hhaallff--dduupplleexx modes are supported.

     The mmsskk driver supports the following media options:

     ffuullll--dduupplleexx  Force full duplex operation.

     hhaallff--dduupplleexx  Force half duplex operation.

     For more information on configuring this device, see ifconfig(8).

